{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPORTANT mechanism discovered while producing story B's evidence: a plan-review gate run pins its CODE read-root to an ATTESTED SNAPSHOT at [snapshot].ref (origin/main HEAD by default) - llm/config.py::resolve_code_root - so it reads .rebar/criteria_routing.json from origin/main, NOT the working tree. My first evidence run therefore never ran the new criterion at all (coverage.routing listed project.portability but not project.symbol-reference-completeness; verified_at_sha a20ccd89b = origin/main HEAD, which has since advanced from 7fc96b277). Fix: 'rebar review-plan --source local' reads the in-place checkout (dirty allowed, never signs) - that is the correct pre-land evidence path, so no early land is needed for AC5. Same mechanism means story A's plan review must use '--ref HEAD', or the reviewer will read a snapshot predating C's .claude/settings.json and emit false 'does not exist' findings. Story B committed as the 3rd change in the stack (63302b487). Two evidence runs now in flight with --source local: the real 061c S1 ticket (7468) and a purpose-built demo ticket (4b14, electric-draconic-vipersquid) whose Scope deliberately hand-enumerates only 2 of the 4 files that mention _anthropic_cache_settings - omitting the monkeypatch.setattr site, i.e. exactly the LSP blind spot. Gerrit: 1016 (C) is now LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1; 1017 (D) CI in progress. Landing plan: close C+D once both are Verified, then review A with --ref HEAD, claim, implement, push, and land the whole stack at the end."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785378140504831001,"uuid":"4bcfedbe-ac76-4094-b45b-a4b06cdf9fee"}